THREE THINGS WORTH KEEPING FROM THIS.

  THE DOMINO IS THE BIG ONE, 1 -> 4486. That is not a surprise once stated: a 1x2 rectangle whose
  long side may be met by two short ones is the BRICK WALL, and running bond, stack bond, herringbone
  and every other bond are exactly the non-edge-to-edge domino tilings. The old board had the single
  stack-bond tiling because that is the only bond that is edge-to-edge.

  THE PENTAGON GAINS NOTHING, 8 -> 8, all eight preserved and no new ones to k=4. Its two sides of
  length 2 decompose arithmetically, but no vertex figure can use the division: the corners that
  flank a unit side are 108 and 90, and 180 is reachable from neither pair. So the half-pentagon
  result published in v1.26.0 is correct as it stands, and it is the only one of the four that is.

  THE HALF-OCTAGON STAYS DEAD, 0 at every k<=4 even with all three of its length-2 sides divisible.
  It was ruled out by the edge-slot parity argument, which assumes each edge is shared by exactly two
  corners and therefore does not apply here; the board had to be re-run rather than argued about, and
  the re-run agrees with the old conclusion for a different reason.

--- RUN 6: tri45all, Marek's own picture --------------------------------------------------------
tri45all is S=1, H=sqrt2, D=2 with T1 (S,H,S), T2 (H,D,H), Q1 and Q2. D = S+S is the only length that
decomposes, so T2's hypotenuse is the only divisible edge: [6,3,3] (H,D,H) -> [6,3,12,3] (H,S,S,H).
That IS the picture he drew: a right triangle whose hypotenuse is met by two smaller triangles' legs.

  k=1 : 17    (was 16)
  k=2 : 227   (was 161)
  k=3 : 2057  (was 1132)
  total 2301  (was 1309)   all 1309 preserved, 992 NEW

A BUG IN MY OWN CHECK, worth writing down because it nearly became a false finding. The first
containment run reported 96 tri45all tilings MISSING from the split set, which would have meant the
remodelling loses tilings and cannot ship. It does not. My congruence oracle computed a face's
"shape" from the CCW turn at each corner, and a MIRRORED transform flips every interior angle to
360-theta, so a face compared across a reflection never matched its twin. Every one of the 96 was a
tiling whose only congruence with its split twin is a mirror. Normalising each face to CCW before
fingerprinting fixes it, and the same rerun then finds all 1309.
  Checked the other boards after the fix: their numbers do not move, because they had already
  reported 0 missing and a false NEGATIVE can only ever inflate that count.
  The oracle in scripts/build-euhalf-shelf.mjs is a different implementation and is not affected;
  this was a bug in the throwaway comparison script, not in anything shipped.

FINAL CONTAINMENT, all boards, after the fix
